  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 150eb (Premium) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>Enhances:</strong> All Bulletproof Shields</p>\n<p><em>By widening a shield’s surface area, one user can protect entire squads.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Shield Enhancement.</strong> Cannot be equipped to any Bulletproof Shield installed in a Popup Shield, and the modified Shield now cannot be installed in a Popup Shield. While wielding the shield, if a character within 2m/yds of the user is targeted with a Ranged Attack, the user may choose to interpose their shield with the Attack (Which interacts with the Shield’s HP as normal), even if it is not their Turn. On the user’s next Turn, they suffer a -1 MOVE penalty (Minimum 2) per Attack that is interposed in this manner.</p>\n<p><strong>Type:</strong> Shield Enhancement<br>\n<strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 0</p>\n<p><strong>Foundry notes:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Shield Attachments and Enhancements follow the Armor Attachment and Enhancement rules, but for Bulletproof Shields, including cyberware ones; not for vehicle Bulletproof Glass. Corgo's optional rule: a Bulletproof Shield with HP left puts its wielder in Cover and counts as a 2x2m/yds piece of Cover against Suppressive Fire, which they may share with one adjacent character.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Armor &amp; Fashion &gt; Shields).</em></p>"
  },
